// HTTP/3 on actors, the server's endpoint and its connections' transport half (stage 5 of the HTTP
// re-architecture, row Q3; the spec, sections 2 and 5). An H3Endpoint is one actor per server UDP socket: it
// receives, reads each datagram's Destination Connection ID through the plug-in's acceptor (header reads
// only) and sends the datagram to the actor of the connection it names, or decides whether an Initial with an
// unknown ID may begin one. It never does protocol work: it does not call 'datagramIn', does not accept and
// does not decrypt. Each connection is an H3ConnActor, made by the endpoint for an admitted Initial, which
// accepts that Initial itself, holds the connection's value (httpclient.H3ServerConn, made by the plug-in:
// this package imports no QUIC), its one Timer and a UdpSender on the endpoint's socket, and runs on whatever
// worker has it. Nothing of QUIC runs on the I/O thread. (netmsg's Endpoint is the model for the receive, the
// owed buffers, the admission bucket and the closing.)
//
// A DATAGRAM'S PATH. The endpoint's receive takes a batch (up to 64, one DatagramBatch kept for its life).
// Each filled buffer is swapped for a fresh one (IoBuf.tryMake: a peer causes these buffers, so a full pool
// refuses one, and the slot stays owed and is filled before the next receive; the kernel drops meanwhile and
// QUIC resends). A buffer's key is looked up in the table:
//   known       the buffer goes to that connection actor as one message ('datagram'), unless the connection
//               already has 'maxBacklog' of them waiting (then it is dropped and counted: unrouted by backlog)
//   unknown Initial   admission, below
//   anything else    dropped and counted (stats.unknownId)
//
// THE TABLE. A Dict from connection ID (httpclient.H3Cid) to a slot in a list of slots (swap-remove: the last
// slot moves into a gap and its keys are pointed at the new place). A slot holds two kinds of key: the
// client's first Destination ID, kept for the connection's life (its resent Initials carry it), and the IDs
// the connection has issued. A key already in the table is never replaced (a refusal counted: stats.idRefused)
// and the issued ones a slot holds are at most 'maxIssuedIds' (stats.idsCapped for the rest), so the table
// holds at most (1 + maxIssuedIds) keys a connection, and a connection's keys leave with it.
//
// REGISTERING ISSUED IDS, WITHOUT THE RACE. A connection learns the IDs it answers to when it accepts and
// again each time the value's idsEpoch moves (a NEW_CONNECTION_ID, a retirement). Before it sends any datagram
// after a move it AWAITS 'ep.ids(id, keys)', answered once the table holds them: so no datagram carrying a new
// ID reaches the client before the endpoint can route the client's answer to it. The client's own first ID is
// registered by the endpoint at admission (it is the Initial's own).
//
// ADMISSION, for an Initial with an unknown ID, in this order, the first limit met refusing it as a drop
// counted by reason: 'accepting' (the endpoint has not been shut down), 'maxConnections', 'maxHandshaking'
// (connections whose handshake is not done), 'maxPerAddress' (by IP address: the source address is forged
// freely for an Initial, so with no Retry this cap holds only for honest sources, and 'maxHandshaking' is the
// bound a flood meets), then an admission rate (a token bucket: 'admitRate' a second, a burst of
// 'admitBurst' seconds of it). The bucket is taken from only when the others pass.
//
// A HANDSHAKING PLACE is held from admission until the connection tells the endpoint 'established' (its
// handshake is done) or 'gone' (it ended). The handshake's own deadline is quic.Config.handshakeTimeout
// (set in the value: the plug-in's server Context): a connection that misses it ends, and 'gone' gives its
// place back. Without it a peer that keeps sending packets that decrypt (anyone can form Initial keys) keeps
// a half-open connection for as long as it likes.
//
// A CONNECTION ACTOR'S TURN. 'datagram' feeds one datagram to the value (or the Timer's wake calls
// handleTimeout), then 'drive' runs the turn: each pass starts the value's turn (startTurn), takes its events,
// then takeDatagram until None, each datagram sent by 'await tx.sendTo(peer, buf)' on the connection's own
// worker; passes go on while something moved or the value still owes a turn (wantsTurn), then the Timer is set to
// the value's pollTimeout. One drive runs at a time: a message that arrives while it is awaiting a send feeds the
// value and asks for another round ('again'). The connection ends as stage 3's ConnActor does ('finishEnd':
// the endpoint is told 'gone', the Timer stopped, the value dropped) and carries a guard so a test can see
// it freed (liveH3ConnActors).
//
// THE HANDLER HALF. A connection of an endpoint a routed server owns (H3Serving) serves its requests through
// serverexchanges.cone, the code ConnActor uses (the connection value is held through h3adapt.cone's adapter). An endpoint
// a program starts itself (startH3Endpoint) has no routes: every request is answered 503 and its request stream reset
// (STOP_SENDING), as a full server answers one.
//
// CLOSING. 'shutdown' stops admitting, asks every connection to shut down (HTTP/3's GOAWAY, then the close),
// waits for them up to 'shutdownTimeout', cancels the group (which ends every connection's sends and Timer and
// the receive) and drops the socket, which closes it.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// What a program may count: actors alive
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// A held counter of the actors that exist: its 'final' runs when the actor's state is freed
struct H3LiveGuard is Move {
  conn: bool;

  fn final(self: &uni) {
    if conn {liveH3Conns.sub(1u64);} else {liveH3Endpoints.sub(1u64);}
  }
}

// How many H3ConnActors exist now (made, and not yet freed)
pub fn liveH3ConnActors() u64 {liveH3Conns.load()}

// How many H3Endpoint actors exist now
pub fn liveH3EndpointActors() u64 {liveH3Endpoints.load()}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Configuration and counters
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// An endpoint's bounds (the defaults are the spec's section 9.4; every one is a field so a program or a test
// may set it)
pub struct H3EndpointConfig {
  pub maxConnections: usize;      // connections held at once (past it, a new Initial is refused)
  pub maxHandshaking: usize;      // connections whose handshake is not done (past it, refused)
  pub maxPerAddress: usize;       // connections one IP address holds (past it, refused)
  pub admitRate: u32;             // new connections a second the endpoint admits (0: no limit)
  pub admitBurst: u32;            // the seconds of 'admitRate' the bucket holds (a burst)
  pub maxBacklog: u32;            // datagrams waiting at one connection (past it, dropped)
  pub shutdownTimeout: Duration;  // how long a shutdown waits for the connections to close before it cuts them

  // The defaults: as many connections as the buffer pool allows by h3driver's own rule (its Config.make: a
  // request stream costs two smallest blocks and a connection 20 more streams, about 51 at the 64 MiB pool),
  // 64 handshaking, 32 an address, 200 a second with a burst of 2 s, 128 datagrams waiting, a 5 s shutdown
  pub fn make() H3EndpointConfig {
    let pool = (stats().maxBytes / 4usize) * 3usize;
    let streams = pool / (2usize * page);
    var perConn = streams / 16usize;
    if perConn > 100usize {perConn = 100usize;}
    if perConn < 4usize {perConn = 4usize;}
    var conns = streams / (perConn + 20usize);
    if conns < 1usize {conns = 1usize;}
    if conns > 10000usize {conns = 10000usize;}
    H3EndpointConfig(conns, 64usize, 32usize, 200u32, 2u32, 128u32, Duration.fromSeconds(5i64))
  }
}

// What an endpoint has refused or dropped, by reason (every counter is cumulative)
pub struct H3EndpointStats {
  pub admitted: u64;              // Initials that began a connection
  pub refusedNotAccepting: u64;   // Initials after the endpoint stopped admitting
  pub refusedFull: u64;           // Initials refused at maxConnections
  pub refusedHandshaking: u64;    // refused at maxHandshaking
  pub refusedPerAddress: u64;     // refused at maxPerAddress for their IP address
  pub refusedRate: u64;           // refused by the admission rate
  pub unknownId: u64;             // datagrams with an ID no connection has, and not an Initial (or not a QUIC packet)
  pub backlogDropped: u64;        // datagrams for a connection that already had maxBacklog waiting
  pub idRefused: u64;             // issued IDs not registered because the table already held the key
  pub idsCapped: u64;             // issued IDs not registered because a connection already had maxIssuedIds
  pub recvRefused: u64;           // receive buffers the buffer pool refused (IoBuf.tryMake): the slot is owed
  pub acceptFailed: u64;          // admitted Initials the acceptor then refused (not a client's first packet, an address that is not IPv4)
  pub tooLong: u64;               // datagrams cut at the receive buffer's size, dropped

  fn none() H3EndpointStats {H3EndpointStats(0u64, 0u64, 0u64, 0u64, 0u64, 0u64, 0u64, 0u64, 0u64, 0u64, 0u64, 0u64, 0u64)}
}

// The most IDs one connection has registered besides its client's first (a peer's active_connection_id_limit
// is small, and QUIC's core issues at most that many)
const maxIssuedIds = 16usize;

// What a connection's 'idsSent' is before it has registered any: no epoch the value has, so the first datagram
// always waits for the first registration
const unreadEpoch = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFu64;

// The room asked of the pool for each receive: its smallest buffer holds 4 KiB; a datagram QUIC sends is at most
// 1452 bytes (quic.defaultMaxUdpPayload), so a longer one is cut and dropped
const recvRoom = 2048usize;
const serverBatch = 64u32;
const maxFailures = 1000u32;
const owedStepMillis = 10i64;

// The admission bucket holds this many seconds of admitRate
const nanosPerSecond = 1000000000i64;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The endpoint
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// A connection an endpoint holds
struct H3Slot {
  id: u64;                          // its number (stable; the slot's index is not)
  conn: H3ConnActor;
  ip: String;                       // the address its peer counts under
  handshaking: bool;                // holds a handshaking place
  keys: List[httpclient.H3Cid];     // [0] the client's first Destination ID, then the issued IDs registered
  backlog: Arc[imm, Atomic[u32]];   // datagrams sent to it and not yet taken by it
}

alias H3Slots = List[H3Slot];
alias H3Table = Dict[httpclient.H3Cid, usize];
alias H3ByConn = Dict[u64, usize];
alias H3ByIp = Dict[String, u32];

// An endpoint bound to a UDP port: the actor to shut down, and the port the socket has
pub struct H3BoundEndpoint {
  pub endpoint: H3Endpoint;
  pub port: u16;
  bound: SocketAddr;

  // The address the socket is bound to, with the port the system chose
  pub fn localAddress(self: &) SocketAddr {bound}
}

pub actor H3Endpoint {
  acc: Arc[imm, Uni[httpclient.H3Acceptor]];
  cfg: H3EndpointConfig;
  sock: UdpSocket;                  // bound by 'open'; UdpSocket.none() before, and after shutdown
  bound: SocketAddr;
  group: CancelGroup;               // cancelled by shutdown: ends the receive and every connection's sends and Timer
  slots: H3Slots;
  table: H3Table;                   // every key to its slot's index
  byConn: H3ByConn;                 // connection number to its slot's index
  byIp: H3ByIp;                     // each IP address's connection count
  handshaking: usize;               // handshaking places held
  tokens: i64;                      // the admission bucket, in thousandths of a connection
  refilled: i64;
  nextConn: u64;
  accepting: bool;
  stopped: bool;
  idsDelayMs: i64;                  // a test's: each 'ids' takes effect this long after it arrives
  refused: H3EndpointStats;
  serving: Option[H3Serving];       // the server that owns this endpoint (its routes serve the requests), or None
  guard: H3LiveGuard;

  fn init(self: &new, acc: Arc[imm, Uni[httpclient.H3Acceptor]], cfg: H3EndpointConfig, serving: Option[H3Serving]) {
    liveH3Endpoints.add(1u64);
    *self = Self(acc: acc, cfg: cfg, sock: UdpSocket.none(), bound: SocketAddr.localhost(0u16), group: CancelGroup.make(),
      slots: H3Slots(), table: H3Table(), byConn: H3ByConn(), byIp: H3ByIp(), handshaking: 0usize,
      tokens: i64.from(cfg.admitBurst) * 1000i64 * i64.from(cfg.admitRate), refilled: Instant.now().nanos(),
      nextConn: 1u64, accepting: true, stopped: false, idsDelayMs: 0i64, refused: H3EndpointStats.none(), serving: serving,
      guard: H3LiveGuard(false));
  }

  // How many connections are held now
  pub async fn connections(self) u32 {u32.from(slots.len())}

  // How many of them have not finished their handshake
  pub async fn handshakingNow(self) u32 {u32.from(handshaking)}

  // How many connection IDs the table holds (every slot's keys)
  pub async fn tableSize(self) u64 {u64.from(table.len())}

  // What the endpoint has refused and dropped so far, by reason
  pub async fn stats(self) H3EndpointStats {refused}

  // FOR TESTS. From now on each registration of a connection's issued IDs takes effect 'ms' milliseconds after it
  // arrives, with the endpoint taking other messages and datagrams meanwhile: the race the connection's
  // awaiting of 'ids' closes (a datagram carrying a just-issued ID arriving before the endpoint knows it)
  pub async fn delayIds(self, ms: i64) {idsDelayMs = ms;}

  // Stop admitting, close the connections (each says GOAWAY, then closes), wait up to the shutdown timeout for
  // them, cut what is left, and close the socket. Call it before the program ends
  pub async fn shutdown(self) {
    let z = await self.stopAll();
  }

  // 'shutdown', answered once the endpoint is closed (the server owning it waits for that)
  async fn stopAll(self) bool {
    if stopped {return true;}
    stopped = true;
    accepting = false;
    var i = 0usize;
    while i < slots.len() {
      slots[i].conn.closeDown();
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
    let limit = Instant.now() + cfg.shutdownTimeout;
    while slots.len() > 0usize && Instant.now() < limit {
      let z = await aio.sleep(Duration.fromMillis(2i64));
    }
    let c = group.cancel();
    sock = UdpSocket.none();
    true
  }

  // ------------------------------------------------------------------
  // The socket
  // ------------------------------------------------------------------

  // Bind the socket at 'bind', say what it got (the address, with the port the system chose when port 0 was
  // asked) or why it could not, then receive. The first message the endpoint is sent
  async fn open(self, bind: SocketAddr, up: OneshotSender[Result[SocketAddr, IoError]]) {
    var tx = up;
    let made = await aio.bindUdp(bind);
    var failure = IoError.ofKind(IoErrorKind.Other);
    match made {
      case let Ok(ok) {sock = ok;}
      case let Err(e) {failure = e;}
    }
    if sock.isNone() {
      tx.send(Err[SocketAddr, IoError](failure));
      return;
    }
    bound = bind;
    let la = await sock.localAddr();
    match &la {
      case let &Ok(a) {bound = *a;}
      else {}
    }
    tx.send(Ok[SocketAddr, IoError](bound));
    selfactor.receive();
  }

  // The server's opening of its endpoint: the same as 'open', answered as the call's value
  async fn openAt(self, bind: SocketAddr) Result[SocketAddr, IoError] {
    let made = await aio.bindUdp(bind);
    match made {
      case let Ok(ok) {sock = ok;}
      case let Err(e) {return Err[SocketAddr, IoError](e);}
    }
    bound = bind;
    let la = await sock.localAddr();
    match &la {
      case let &Ok(a) {bound = *a;}
      else {}
    }
    selfactor.receive();
    Ok[SocketAddr, IoError](bound)
  }

  fn servingCopy(self: &) Option[H3Serving] {
    match &serving {
      case let &Some(s) {Some[H3Serving](H3Serving(s.srv, s.args))}
      else {None[H3Serving]}
    }
  }

  // Receive datagrams until shutdown cancels the receive: the next and any already waiting (up to the batch), each
  // handled in place in arrival order. The batch is kept for the endpoint's life; each filled buffer is swapped
  // out of its slot for a fresh one and sent on. A buffer the pool refuses leaves its slot owed, and no receive
  // starts while one is owed
  async fn receive(self) {
    var failures = 0u32;
    var batch = DatagramBatch.make(serverBatch, recvRoom);
    while !stopped && failures <= maxFailures {
      var owedSlot = batch.firstWithoutRoom();
      while owedSlot != 0xFFFFFFFFu32 {
        match IoBuf.tryMake(recvRoom) {
          case var Some(b) {
            let old = batch.swapOut(owedSlot, b);
            owedSlot = batch.firstWithoutRoom();
          }
          else {
            refused.recvRefused = refused.recvRefused + 1u64;
            let z = await aio.sleep(Duration.fromMillis(owedStepMillis));
            if stopped {return;}
          }
        }
      }
      let r = await sock.recvManyIn(batch, IoLimits.within(group));
      match r {
        case var Ok(ok) {
          failures = 0u32;
          batch = ok;
          let cnt = batch.count();
          var k = 0u32;
          while k < cnt {
            let from = batch.from(k);
            var fresh = IoBuf();
            match IoBuf.tryMake(recvRoom) {
              case var Some(b) {fresh = b;}
              else {refused.recvRefused = refused.recvRefused + 1u64;}
            }
            let buf = batch.swapOut(k, fresh);
            if batch.wasCut(k) {
              refused.tooLong = refused.tooLong + 1u64;
            } else {
              self.onDatagram(from, buf);
            }
            k = k + 1u32;
          }
        }
        case var Err(f) {
          let e, back = f.(error, batch);
          match back {
            case var Some(b) {batch = b;}
            else {batch = DatagramBatch.make(serverBatch, recvRoom);}
          }
          if aio.isCancelled(e) {return;}
          if !aio.isTruncated(e) {failures = failures + 1u32;}
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // ------------------------------------------------------------------
  // From the connections
  // ------------------------------------------------------------------

  // A connection's handshake is done: its handshaking place is given back
  async fn established(self, conn: u64) {
    match byConn.getCopy(&conn) {
      case let Some(k) {
        if slots[k].handshaking {
          slots[k].handshaking = false;
          handshaking = handshaking - 1usize;
        }
      }
      else {}
    }
  }

  // A connection has ended (or its accept was refused): its keys leave the table, its place is given back
  async fn gone(self, conn: u64, acceptFailed: bool) {
    if acceptFailed {refused.acceptFailed = refused.acceptFailed + 1u64;}
    match byConn.getCopy(&conn) {
      case let Some(k) {self.removeSlot(k);}
      else {}
    }
  }

  // The connection's issued IDs (all it answers to now except the client's first), registered once the table
  // holds them: the connection awaits this answer before it sends a datagram that carries a new one. A key the
  // table already holds (for any connection) is not replaced; the slot holds at most maxIssuedIds
  async fn ids(self, conn: u64, keys: List[httpclient.H3Cid]) bool {
    if idsDelayMs > 0i64 {
      let z = await aio.sleep(Duration.fromMillis(idsDelayMs));
    }
    let Some(k) = byConn.getCopy(&conn) else {return false;};
    // The keys the connection no longer answers to leave; the kept ones stay
    var i = 1usize;
    while i < slots[k].keys.len() {
      if hasKey(&keys, &slots[k].keys[i]) {
        i = i + 1usize;
      } else {
        let gone = table.remove(&slots[k].keys[i]);
        let dropped = slots[k].keys.swapRemove(i);
      }
    }
    var n = 0usize;
    while n < keys.len() {
      let key = keys[n];
      n = n + 1usize;
      if hasKey(&slots[k].keys, &key) {continue;}
      if slots[k].keys.len() > maxIssuedIds {
        refused.idsCapped = refused.idsCapped + 1u64;
        continue;
      }
      if table.contains(&key) {
        refused.idRefused = refused.idRefused + 1u64;
        continue;
      }
      table.insert(key, k);
      slots[k].keys.push(key);
    }
    true
  }

  // ------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Inside
  // ------------------------------------------------------------------

  // A datagram arrived, from 'from'
  fn onDatagram(self, from: SocketAddr, buf: IoBuf) {
    // (after a shutdown has begun, a known connection's datagrams still go to it so it can finish closing, and an
    // Initial is refused by 'accepting')
    let Some(key) = acc.connectionId(buf.view()) else {
      refused.unknownId = refused.unknownId + 1u64;
      return;
    };
    match table.getCopy(&key) {
      case let Some(k) {
        self.deliver(k, buf);
        return;
      }
      else {}
    }
    if !acc.isInitial(buf.view()) {
      refused.unknownId = refused.unknownId + 1u64;
      return;
    }
    self.admit(from, key, buf);
  }

  // The datagram to slot k's connection, unless it has maxBacklog waiting
  fn deliver(self, k: usize, buf: IoBuf) {
    if slots[k].backlog.add(1u32) >= cfg.maxBacklog {
      let back = slots[k].backlog.sub(1u32);
      refused.backlogDropped = refused.backlogDropped + 1u64;
      return;
    }
    slots[k].conn.datagram(buf);
  }

  // An Initial with an unknown ID: the limits in order, then a connection actor that accepts it
  fn admit(self, from: SocketAddr, key: httpclient.H3Cid, first: IoBuf) {
    if !accepting {
      refused.refusedNotAccepting = refused.refusedNotAccepting + 1u64;
      return;
    }
    if slots.len() >= cfg.maxConnections {
      refused.refusedFull = refused.refusedFull + 1u64;
      return;
    }
    if handshaking >= cfg.maxHandshaking {
      refused.refusedHandshaking = refused.refusedHandshaking + 1u64;
      return;
    }
    let ip = ipOf(&from);
    if self.connsOf(ip.view()) >= cfg.maxPerAddress {
      refused.refusedPerAddress = refused.refusedPerAddress + 1u64;
      return;
    }
    if !self.takeToken(Instant.now().nanos()) {
      refused.refusedRate = refused.refusedRate + 1u64;
      return;
    }
    refused.admitted = refused.admitted + 1u64;
    let id = nextConn;
    nextConn = nextConn + 1u64;
    let backlog = Arc[imm, Atomic[u32]](Atomic[u32].of(0u32));
    let conn = H3ConnActor(id, selfactor, acc, bound, from, sock.sender(), group, backlog, self.servingCopy());
    var keys = List[httpclient.H3Cid]();
    keys.push(key);
    let k = slots.len();
    slots.push(H3Slot(id, conn, String.from(ip.view()), true, keys, backlog));
    table.insert(key, k);
    byConn.insert(id, k);
    handshaking = handshaking + 1usize;
    self.joinIp(ip.view());
    conn.begin(first);
  }

  // Take slot k out: its keys leave the table, the last slot moves into the gap and its entries are pointed there
  fn removeSlot(self, k: usize) {
    var i = 0usize;
    while i < slots[k].keys.len() {
      let gone = table.remove(&slots[k].keys[i]);
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
    if slots[k].handshaking {handshaking = handshaking - 1usize;}
    let ip = String.from(slots[k].ip.view());
    self.leaveIp(ip.view());
    let id = slots[k].id;
    let gone = byConn.remove(&id);
    let last = slots.len() - 1usize;
    if k != last {
      slots.swap(k, last);
    }
    let dropped = slots.pop();
    if k != last {
      byConn.insert(slots[k].id, k);
      var j = 0usize;
      while j < slots[k].keys.len() {
        table.insert(slots[k].keys[j], k);
        j = j + 1usize;
      }
    }
  }

  fn joinIp(self, ip: &str) {
    match byIp.getMut(ip) {
      case let Some(a) {*a = *a + 1u32; return;}
      else {}
    }
    byIp.insert(String.from(ip), 1u32);
  }

  // (the table holds only addresses with a connection)
  fn leaveIp(self, ip: &str) {
    var last = false;
    match byIp.getMut(ip) {
      case let Some(a) {
        *a = *a - 1u32;
        last = *a == 0u32;
      }
      else {}
    }
    if last {
      let dropped = byIp.remove(ip);
    }
  }

  fn connsOf(self: &, ip: &str) usize {
    match byIp.get(ip) {
      case let Some(a) {return usize.from(*a);}
      else {}
    }
    0usize
  }

  // One connection's worth from the admission bucket, refilled by the time since it was last looked at, holding no
  // more than admitBurst seconds of it. False when it holds less than one. A rate of 0 is no limit
  fn takeToken(self, now: i64) bool {
    if cfg.admitRate == 0u32 {return true;}
    let per = i64.from(cfg.admitRate);
    let longest = i64.from(cfg.admitBurst) * nanosPerSecond;
    let gap = now - refilled;
    if gap >= longest {
      tokens = i64.from(cfg.admitBurst) * 1000i64 * per;
      refilled = now;
    } else if gap >= 1000000i64 {
      let ms = gap / 1000000i64;
      tokens = tokens + ms * per;
      refilled = refilled + ms * 1000000i64;
    }
    let cap = i64.from(cfg.admitBurst) * 1000i64 * per;
    if tokens > cap {tokens = cap;}
    if tokens < 1000i64 {return false;}
    tokens = tokens - 1000i64;
    true
  }
}

// Whether 'keys' holds 'k'
fn hasKey(keys: &List[httpclient.H3Cid], k: &httpclient.H3Cid) bool {
  var i = 0usize;
  while i < keys.len() {
    if keys[i] == *k {return true;}
    i = i + 1usize;
  }
  false
}

// The text a peer's connections are counted under: its IP address, the port left out ("a.b.c.d:port", or
// "[...]:port" for IPv6, whose whole address is the key: QUIC here is IPv4 alone)
fn ipOf(addr: &SocketAddr) String {
  let t = addr.text();
  let v = t.view();
  var cut = v.len();
  var i = v.len();
  while i > 0usize {
    i = i - 1usize;
    if v[i] == 58u8 {cut = i; break;}
  }
  String.from(v.slice(0usize, cut))
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Starting one
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Binding takes a second worker when the caller is one: the endpoint binds on the I/O thread and answers from
// a worker, and the call waits for it
fn requireAWorker() {
  if actors.workerIndex() != actors.noWorker && actors.stats().workers < 2u32 {
    panic("actorhttp: startH3Endpoint called from a behaviour needs a second worker to bind the socket");
  }
}

// An HTTP/3 endpoint on the UDP socket bound at 'bind' (port 0: the system chooses, and 'port' says which), its
// connections made by 'acceptor' (the plug-in's: Http3.acceptor), under 'cfg's limits: the endpoint, or why the
// socket could not be bound. Every connection answers its requests 503 (a routed server's server actor makes its own
// endpoint, and its connections serve its routes). Call 'endpoint.shutdown()' before the program ends
pub fn startH3Endpoint(bind: SocketAddr, acceptor: Uni[httpclient.H3Acceptor], cfg: H3EndpointConfig)
    Result[H3BoundEndpoint, IoError] {
  requireAWorker();
  let ep = H3Endpoint(Arc[imm, Uni[httpclient.H3Acceptor]](acceptor), cfg, None[H3Serving]);
  var tx: OneshotSender[Result[SocketAddr, IoError]];
  var rx: OneshotReceiver[Result[SocketAddr, IoError]];
  tx, rx = Oneshot[Result[SocketAddr, IoError]].make();
  ep.open(bind, tx);
  let Some(answer) = rx.recv() else {return Err[H3BoundEndpoint, IoError](IoError.aborted());};
  let a = answer?;
  Ok[H3BoundEndpoint, IoError](H3BoundEndpoint(ep, a.port(), a))
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// A server connection's actor: the transport half
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// The datagrams a turn sends before it takes breath (and asks the value to finish its turn)
const sendBurst = 64usize;

// What a server owning an endpoint gives each connection: the server (its queue route and its end) and what it was
// listened with (its routes and bounds)
struct H3Serving {
  srv: ServerActor;
  args: Arc[imm, ListenArgs];
}

// A queue-route connection's number, apart from every TCP connection's the server numbers (their counter would need
// 2^63 connections to reach it)
const h3QueueBit = 0x8000000000000000u64;

// The transport half of a QUIC server connection: datagrams in from the endpoint, the value's datagrams out, one Timer.
// What a request is, its handler and its response is the handler half's (serverexchanges.cone, the same code as
// ConnActor's), which this actor holds when a server owns the endpoint. An endpoint a program starts on its own
// (startH3Endpoint) has no routes: its connections answer every request 503 and reset its stream
actor H3ConnActor is ExchangeHost {
  id: u64;
  ep: Option[H3Endpoint];
  acc: Arc[imm, Uni[httpclient.H3Acceptor]];
  bound: SocketAddr;
  peer: SocketAddr;
  tx: UdpSender;
  group: CancelGroup;
  backlog: Arc[imm, Atomic[u32]];     // datagrams the endpoint has sent and this actor has not taken
  conn: Option[H3ServerAdapter];      // the value (its Uni inside), made at 'begin'
  hx: Option[ServerExchanges[H3ServerAdapter]];    // the handler half, when a server owns the endpoint
  tm: actors.Timer;
  driving: bool;                      // a drive is running (it awaits sends)
  again: bool;                        // input arrived while it ran: another round
  timerDue: bool;                     // the Timer woke it: the next pass is one a timer began
  told: bool;                         // the endpoint has been told the handshake is done
  ended: bool;
  idsSent: u64;                       // the value's idsEpoch the endpoint holds the IDs of
  guard: H3LiveGuard;

  fn init(self: &new, id: u64, ep: H3Endpoint, acc: Arc[imm, Uni[httpclient.H3Acceptor]], bound: SocketAddr,
      peer: SocketAddr, tx: UdpSender, group: CancelGroup, backlog: Arc[imm, Atomic[u32]], serving: Option[H3Serving]) {
    liveH3Conns.add(1u64);
    var hx = None[ServerExchanges[H3ServerAdapter]];
    match &serving {
      case let &Some(s) {
        hx = Some[ServerExchanges[H3ServerAdapter]](
          ServerExchanges[H3ServerAdapter].make(id | h3QueueBit, s.srv, s.args, peer, true, true, String()));
      }
      else {}
    }
    *self = Self(id: id, ep: Some[H3Endpoint](ep), acc: acc, bound: bound, peer: peer, tx: tx, group: group,
      backlog: backlog, conn: None[H3ServerAdapter], hx: hx, tm: actors.Timer.within(&group), driving: false,
      again: false, timerDue: false, told: false, ended: false, idsSent: unreadEpoch, guard: H3LiveGuard(true));
  }

  // The value out of its place, for a call that needs it beside the handler half (and 'putConn' to give it back)
  fn takeConn(self) Option[H3ServerAdapter] {
    var held = None[H3ServerAdapter];
    held <-> conn;
    held
  }

  fn putConn(self, held: Option[H3ServerAdapter]) {
    var h = held;
    conn <-> h;
  }

  // The connection's first message: its Initial, accepted here (the endpoint does no protocol work)
  pub async fn begin(self, first: IoBuf) {
    let now = Instant.now();
    match acc.accept(first.view(), bound, peer, now) {
      case var Ok(c) {conn = Some[H3ServerAdapter](H3ServerAdapter.make(c));}
      case let Err(f) {
        self.finishEnd(true);
        return;
      }
    }
    selfactor.timerLoop();
    selfactor.drive();
  }

  // One datagram of this connection's, from the endpoint
  pub async fn datagram(self, buf: IoBuf) {
    let back = backlog.sub(1u32);
    if ended {return;}
    let now = Instant.now();
    var held = self.takeConn();
    match &mut held {
      case let &mut Some(a) {a.conn.datagramIn(buf.view(), now);}
      else {}
    }
    self.putConn(held);
    selfactor.drive();
  }

  // The endpoint is closing: GOAWAY, what is open finishes, then the close
  pub async fn closeDown(self) {
    if ended {return;}
    var held = self.takeConn();
    match &mut held {
      case let &mut Some(a) {a.shutdown();}
      else {}
    }
    self.putConn(held);
    selfactor.drive();
  }

  // The Timer's deadline, for the connection's life: each time it comes the value handles its timeout. It ends
  // when the Timer does (finishEnd stopped it, or the endpoint's group was cancelled)
  pub async fn timerLoop(self) {
    while await tm.next() {
      if ended {break;}
      var held = self.takeConn();
      match &mut held {
        case let &mut Some(a) {a.handleTimeout(Instant.now());}
        else {}
      }
      self.putConn(held);
      timerDue = true;
      selfactor.drive();
    }
    self.finishEnd(false);
  }

  // The turn: the value's events, then its datagrams sent, again until nothing more moves and the value owes no
  // turn. Each pass starts one (startTurn), so an owed turn is taken up once. One drive at a time (a send is
  // awaited, and another message may arrive then: it feeds the value and sets 'again'). Every pass awaits
  // 'sends', itself a message to this actor, so the messages already waiting are handled between passes
  pub async fn drive(self) {
    if driving {
      again = true;
      return;
    }
    driving = true;
    var more = true;
    while more && !ended {
      more = false;
      again = false;
      self.startTurn();
      if self.events() {more = true;}
      let sent = await self.sends();
      if sent {more = true;}
      if again {more = true;}
      if !ended && self.wantsTurn() {more = true;}
    }
    driving = false;
    if !ended {self.settle();}
  }

  fn startTurn(self) {
    let byTimer = timerDue;
    timerDue = false;
    var held = self.takeConn();
    match &mut held {
      case let &mut Some(a) {a.conn.startTurn(byTimer);}
      else {}
    }
    self.putConn(held);
  }

  fn wantsTurn(self) bool {
    var held = self.takeConn();
    var w = false;
    match &mut held {
      case let &mut Some(a) {w = a.conn.wantsTurn();}
      else {}
    }
    self.putConn(held);
    w
  }

  // What the value says, acted on: by the handler half when a server owns the endpoint; else every request is answered
  // 503 and its request stream reset, body bytes are released, the end noted. True when there was an event
  fn events(self) bool {
    let now = Instant.now();
    var any = false;
    var held = self.takeConn();
    match &mut held {
      case let &mut Some(a) {
        match &mut hx {
          case let &mut Some(h) {any = h.events(a, selfactor, now);}
          else {
            // No routes: 'startH3Endpoint' (an endpoint no server owns) answers every request 503 and resets its stream.
            // Only h3driver's tests use it; a routed server's endpoint serves through the handler half above
            var going = true;
            while going {
              match a.next(now) {
                case is Nothing {going = false;}
                case let Request(q) {
                  any = true;
                  let stream = q.stream;
                  let head = a.response();
                  head.status = 503u16;
                  a.respond(stream, BodyLength.sized(0u64));
                  a.finish(stream);
                  let stopped = a.stopBody(stream);
                }
                case let Data(d) {
                  any = true;
                  let st, bf = d.(stream, buf);
                  a.release(st, bf.len());
                }
                case let End(e) {any = true;}
                case let Reset(x) {any = true;}
                case let Closed(x) {any = true;}
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
      else {}
    }
    self.putConn(held);
    any
  }

  // The value's datagrams to the peer, until it has none (or a burst's worth, then the turn is finished). Before a
  // datagram goes, the endpoint holds the IDs the value answers to now. True when anything was sent
  async fn sends(self) bool {
    var sent = false;
    var n = 0usize;
    while !ended {
      let now = Instant.now();
      var out = None[IoBuf];
      var epoch = 0u64;
      var keys = List[httpclient.H3Cid]();
      var held = self.takeConn();
      var present = false;
      match &mut held {
        case let &mut Some(a) {
          present = true;
          if n >= sendBurst {
            a.conn.finishTurn(now);
          } else {
            out = a.conn.takeDatagram(now);
            epoch = a.conn.idsEpoch();
            if epoch != idsSent {let made = a.conn.ids(&mut keys);}
          }
        }
        else {}
      }
      self.putConn(held);
      if !present {break;}
      let Some(buf) = out else {break;};
      if epoch != idsSent {
        // No datagram goes out that may carry an ID the endpoint does not know: the answer comes once the table holds them
        idsSent = epoch;
        match &ep {
          case let &Some(e) {let ok = await e.ids(id, keys);}
          else {}
        }
        if ended {break;}
      }
      // (the send's Result is ignored: a datagram the socket would not take is a lost datagram, which QUIC's loss
      // recovery resends, not an error of this connection's)
      let r = await tx.sendToIn(peer, buf, IoLimits.within(group));
      n = n + 1usize;
      sent = true;
    }
    sent
  }

  // After a drive: the Timer to the value's next wake, the endpoint told when the handshake is done, the end taken
  fn settle(self) {
    let now = Instant.now();
    var done = false;
    var open = false;
    var wake = None[Instant];
    var held = self.takeConn();
    match &mut held {
      case let &mut Some(a) {
        done = a.done(now);
        open = a.isOpen();
        wake = a.pollTimeout();
      }
      else {}
    }
    self.putConn(held);
    match wake {
      case let Some(t) {tm.set(t);}
      else {tm.clear();}
    }
    if open && !told {
      told = true;
      match &ep {
        case let &Some(e) {e.established(id);}
        else {}
      }
    }
    if done {self.finishEnd(false);}
  }

  // The connection is over: every stream is told, the server (if one owns the endpoint) and the endpoint are told, the
  // Timer stopped, the value dropped
  fn finishEnd(self, acceptFailed: bool) {
    if ended {return;}
    ended = true;
    tm.stop();
    var held = self.takeConn();
    match &mut held {
      case let &mut Some(a) {
        match &mut hx {
          case let &mut Some(h) {h.clear(a, selfactor);}
          else {}
        }
      }
      else {}
    }
    held = None[H3ServerAdapter];
    match &hx {
      case let &Some(h) {h.srv.connEnded(h.id);}
      else {}
    }
    hx = None[ServerExchanges[H3ServerAdapter]];
    match &ep {
      case let &Some(e) {e.gone(id, acceptFailed);}
      else {}
    }
    ep = None[H3Endpoint];
  }

  // ---- the Exchange's calls: the handler half's, then a drive

  pub async fn xRespond(self, stream: u32, rid: u64, head: ResponseHead, body: String) {
    var held = self.takeConn();
    match &mut held {
      case let &mut Some(a) {
        match &mut hx {
          case let &mut Some(h) {h.xRespond(a, selfactor, stream, rid, head, body);}
          else {}
        }
      }
      else {}
    }
    self.putConn(held);
    selfactor.drive();
  }

  pub async fn xStart(self, stream: u32, rid: u64, head: ResponseHead, framing: BodyLength) {
    var held = self.takeConn();
    match &mut held {
      case let &mut Some(a) {
        match &mut hx {
          case let &mut Some(h) {h.xStart(a, selfactor, stream, rid, head, framing);}
          else {}
        }
      }
      else {}
    }
    self.putConn(held);
    selfactor.drive();
  }

  pub async fn xWrite(self, stream: u32, rid: u64, data: String, rp: actors.ReplyOf[Result[usize, ServerError]]) {
    var held = self.takeConn();
    match &mut held {
      case let &mut Some(a) {
        match &mut hx {
          case let &mut Some(h) {h.xWrite(a, selfactor, stream, rid, data, rp);}
          else {rp.answer(Err[usize, ServerError](ServerError.closed()));}
        }
      }
      else {rp.answer(Err[usize, ServerError](ServerError.closed()));}
    }
    self.putConn(held);
    selfactor.drive();
  }

  pub async fn xFinish(self, stream: u32, rid: u64, rp: actors.ReplyOf[Result[u64, ServerError]]) {
    var held = self.takeConn();
    match &mut held {
      case let &mut Some(a) {
        match &mut hx {
          case let &mut Some(h) {h.xFinish(a, selfactor, stream, rid, rp);}
          else {rp.answer(Err[u64, ServerError](ServerError.closed()));}
        }
      }
      else {rp.answer(Err[u64, ServerError](ServerError.closed()));}
    }
    self.putConn(held);
    selfactor.drive();
  }

  pub async fn xDrop(self, stream: u32, rid: u64, spare: RequestHead) {
    var held = self.takeConn();
    match &mut held {
      case let &mut Some(a) {
        match &mut hx {
          case let &mut Some(h) {h.xDrop(a, selfactor, stream, rid, spare);}
          else {}
        }
      }
      else {}
    }
    self.putConn(held);
    selfactor.drive();
  }

  pub async fn xBodyRead(self, stream: u32, rid: u64, rp: actors.ReplyOf[Result[Option[String], BodyError]]) {
    var held = self.takeConn();
    match &mut held {
      case let &mut Some(a) {
        match &mut hx {
          case let &mut Some(h) {h.xBodyRead(a, selfactor, stream, rid, rp);}
          else {rp.answer(Err[Option[String], BodyError](BodyError.cancelled()));}
        }
      }
      else {rp.answer(Err[Option[String], BodyError](BodyError.cancelled()));}
    }
    self.putConn(held);
    selfactor.drive();
  }

  pub async fn xBodyAll(self, stream: u32, rid: u64, limit: usize, rp: actors.ReplyOf[Result[String, BodyError]]) {
    var held = self.takeConn();
    match &mut held {
      case let &mut Some(a) {
        match &mut hx {
          case let &mut Some(h) {h.xBodyAll(a, selfactor, stream, rid, limit, rp);}
          else {rp.answer(Err[String, BodyError](BodyError.cancelled()));}
        }
      }
      else {rp.answer(Err[String, BodyError](BodyError.cancelled()));}
    }
    self.putConn(held);
    selfactor.drive();
  }

  pub async fn xBodyTo(self, stream: u32, rid: u64, sink: ChunkSink, src: ChunkSource) {
    var held = self.takeConn();
    match &mut held {
      case let &mut Some(a) {
        match &mut hx {
          case let &mut Some(h) {h.xBodyTo(a, selfactor, stream, rid, sink, src);}
          else {sink.end(Ending.Failed(AnyError.from(BodyError.cancelled())));}
        }
      }
      else {sink.end(Ending.Failed(AnyError.from(BodyError.cancelled())));}
    }
    self.putConn(held);
    selfactor.drive();
  }

  pub async fn xBodyBack(self, stream: u32, rid: u64, b: IoBuf) {
    var held = self.takeConn();
    match &mut held {
      case let &mut Some(a) {
        match &mut hx {
          case let &mut Some(h) {h.xBodyBack(a, selfactor, stream, rid, b);}
          else {}
        }
      }
      else {}
    }
    self.putConn(held);
    selfactor.drive();
  }

  pub async fn xBodyStop(self, stream: u32, rid: u64, why: Ending) {
    var held = self.takeConn();
    match &mut held {
      case let &mut Some(a) {
        match &mut hx {
          case let &mut Some(h) {h.xBodyStop(a, selfactor, stream, rid, why);}
          else {}
        }
      }
      else {}
    }
    self.putConn(held);
    selfactor.drive();
  }

  pub async fn xBodyDrop(self, stream: u32, rid: u64) {
    var held = self.takeConn();
    match &mut held {
      case let &mut Some(a) {
        match &mut hx {
          case let &mut Some(h) {h.xBodyDrop(a, selfactor, stream, rid);}
          else {}
        }
      }
      else {}
    }
    self.putConn(held);
    selfactor.drive();
  }

  pub async fn handOut(self, stream: u32, rid: u64, rp: actors.ReplyOf[Result[Exchange, ServerError]], to: ServerActor) {
    var held = self.takeConn();
    match &mut held {
      case let &mut Some(a) {
        match &mut hx {
          case let &mut Some(h) {h.handOut(a, selfactor, stream, rid, rp, to, ended);}
          else {to.stale(rp);}
        }
      }
      else {to.stale(rp);}
    }
    self.putConn(held);
  }

  pub async fn refuse(self, stream: u32, rid: u64) {
    var held = self.takeConn();
    match &mut held {
      case let &mut Some(a) {
        match &mut hx {
          case let &mut Some(h) {h.refuse(a, selfactor, stream, rid);}
          else {}
        }
      }
      else {}
    }
    self.putConn(held);
    selfactor.drive();
  }
}
